<type>(<scope>): <emoji> <description>

<optional body>

Verified-by: <lint, phpstan, audit>
Refs: #<issue>
Co-authored-by: <name> <email>

# Format enforced by the commitlint/Husky hook (see commitlint.config.js
# and .claude/skills/semantic-commit-messages/) — a message that doesn't
# follow these rules is REJECTED at commit time, not just discouraged:
# - <type>: feat, fix, refactor, perf, style, test, docs, build, ops, chore
#   (no other word, no capitalization, no space inside <type>)
# - <scope> optional: the area of the repo touched (deploy, theme,
#   docker...), never an issue number
# - <emoji>: optional but recommended, at the start of <description>,
#   chosen per <type> — the emoji is part of <description>: commitlint
#   only parses "type(scope):", so this doesn't break validation:
#   [ ] ✨ API/UI feature (feat)
#   [ ] 🐛 API/UI bug fix (fix)
#   [ ] ♻️ Refactoring, no behavior change (refactor)
#   [ ] ⚡ Performance (perf)
#   [ ] 🎨 Style / formatting (style)
#   [ ] ✅ Tests (test)
#   [ ] 📚 Documentation (docs)
#   [ ] 🛠️ Build / dependencies (build)
#   [ ] 🚀 Infra / deployment / CI-CD (ops)
#   [ ] 🧹 Other / housekeeping (chore)
# - <description>: imperative present tense, lowercase, NO trailing period
# - Breaking change: "!" after the type/scope, or a "BREAKING CHANGE: ..."
#   footer
#
# Multi-line body (optional, separated from the subject by a blank line):
# one "- ..." bullet per distinct concern if the commit touches several
# points; otherwise a short paragraph is enough.
#
# Footer trailers below the body, one per line, delete what doesn't apply:
# - Verified-by: comma-separated subset of what you actually ran before
#   committing — check against this list, then write the ones that pass:
#   [ ] make lint     — 0 Pint errors
#   [ ] make phpstan  — 0 errors (level 5)
#   [ ] make audit    — no advisories
# - Refs: GitHub issue number if relevant ("Refs #123", "Closes #123")
# - Co-authored-by: standard git trailer to credit a pair/contributor who
#   isn't the committer (GitHub renders it on the commit) — delete this
#   line entirely if solo
#
# Lines starting with # are stripped and won't be part of the message.
